# Gitignored paths a fresh worktree needs, copied by `wt step copy-ignored`.
# Without this file the step is a no-op: it is gated by `--require-include`.
#
# On APFS these are reflink clones, so 601 MB of pnpm dependencies costs almost
# nothing to provision. Without them a focused test or typecheck fails with a
# missing-module error that reads as broken code rather than an unprovisioned
# checkout.
#
# `target/` is deliberately absent. The user-level `cargo-target` hook points
# CARGO_TARGET_DIR at a shared directory keyed to the primary checkout, and the
# global copy-ignored exclusion drops it, so a 4 GB Rust build tree is neither
# copied nor rebuilt per worktree.
node_modules/
apps/desktop/node_modules/
packages/contracts/node_modules/
